## File-transfer honesty (known defect class)

Broker staging is **not** delivery to the remote. An upload toast that
says the file reached broker staging is **Partial** until a target push
is observed. Do not mark File transfer **Live** from staging success,
a visible panel, or an HTTP 200 on the broker.

## Forbidden “false green”

- SPA-only walk cited as all-platforms
- Windows-only binaries cited as Linux / macOS coverage
- Connect chrome, Jump fleet, or `/options` 200 without protocol surface
- Binder list / tabs / export without sampled section bodies
- Messaging page load without an observed inbox message
- File transfer Live from broker-staging toast
- “Works” from `cargo build`, deploy exit 0, or service RUNNING
  without served-bundle (or equivalent) identity + inspected proof
- Single-seat or SSH-only matrix as “all protocols / all workstations”
- SPA-only German flip cited as all-platforms localization
- Leftover English on DE marked Live because the locale cookie flipped
- New i18n spec invented while `i18n-german-embedded-live.spec.ts` exists
- Tier 1 complete while `en-GB` / `zh-Hans` catalogs are absent
- Invented IGA copy, or unofficial translations of official control bodies

## Worked violation → fix

**Violation.** Campaign reports Connect / File transfer / Binder PASS
from admin-SPA chrome on Windows only. SSH-only seat. File transfer
toast is staging-only. Binder tabs never open a section body. German
is “done” because the locale cookie flipped while headings stayed
English. Two workers edit the same live-session file. A child sits
in “planning next moves”; the parent fans out explore workers.

**Fix.** Inventory every GUI class this run and mark missing Unix
binaries **N/A — no binary**. Protocol-surface (or honest BLOCKED) for
each offered protocol. File transfer stays Partial until target push.
Binder: live session + section bodies ≥ 40 characters, not placeholder.
en ↔ de flip on each class with a locale switch; leftover English →
`t()` + DE packs in the same commit; reuse
`i18n-german-embedded-live.spec.ts`. One writer per file; one deploy
owner. Interrupt the stuck child once, abandon, finish in the parent.

